---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Call a method (a request file, or --target, --method and --data) and print the response

Usage: rustman grpc call [OPTIONS] <REQUEST|--target <TARGET>>

Arguments:
  [REQUEST]
          A grpc request file, its id or its name

Options:
      --target <TARGET>
          The target of an ad-hoc call: host:port, grpc://host:port or grpcs://host:port

      --method <METHOD>
          The method of an ad-hoc call: package.Service/Method

      --data <JSON>
          The request message as JSON (default: {}); a JSON array sends each entry in order (client and bidi streaming)

  -m, --metadata <NAME: VALUE>
          Add request metadata (repeatable): --metadata "authorization: Bearer {{token}}"; names ending in -bin take base64

      --deadline-ms <MS>
          The deadline of an ad-hoc call in milliseconds (default: settings timeout_ms, else 30000)

      --json
          Print each received message as one JSON line, then a final status line

      --env <NAME>
          Environment (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards)

      --var <K=V>
          Set a variable, above every other source (repeatable): --var k=v

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Total timeout per request, replacing settings.timeout_ms: 500ms, 5s, 2m, or a number of milliseconds

  -k, --insecure
          Do not verify TLS certificates (exchanges are flagged insecure)

      --no-history
          Do not record the exchanges in history

      --trace
          Send trace context (traceparent) even when no trace block enables it

  -u, --update-snapshots
          Overwrite snapshots that differ from the response (not in CI mode)

      --ci
          CI mode: never write snapshots, and fail on a missing one (also on when the CI variable is true or 1)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
